#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:93
#: 022b784b9af24c71813f7babe898d385
msgid ":ref:`RSSI_TYPE<RSSI_TYPE>` = 3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:96
#: e068e9488a78453d9b786bc9f4f7bd85
msgid "RC input to Serial Port"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:98
#: 620450d34d46475890c41a255eb5deb8
msgid "any UART RX input will auto-detect all the protocols (except PPM, or SRXL2/CRSF/ELRS which also require connection of the UART's TX pin), if the serial port protocol is set to 23 (for example, generally, :ref:`SERIAL2_PROTOCOL<SERIAL2_PROTOCOL>` for the TELEM2 UART if used). The exception to this is for SBUS attached to UARTs on F4 based autopilots. This requires an external inverter since SBUS is inverted and F4 autopilots do not have selectable inversion on their UART pins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:100
#: c71984d43b53466ab8092698fa16d688
msgid "The serial port baudrate is automatically set and controlled by the firmware when any serial RC protocol is detected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:104
#: 59904ee785db4550996432d295ef440f
msgid "Radio System Selection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:106
#: c3ba4c783c9a4f80a3f0f7975f458bc2
msgid "Selection will depend on many factors: range,telemetry requirements, cost, compatibility with existing equipment, etc. Most manufacturers often many different models with differing capabilities. Many systems have been reverse-engineered and \"cloned\" by other manufacturers offering more economical versions of transmitters and receivers. Many Transmitters offer multiple protocols and are based on the `OpenTX <https://www.open-tx.org/>`__ firmware which is extremely flexible and also allows the use of LUA scripts to display telemetry data on their LCD screens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:109
#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:134
#: ee53742faaa14a6d9d9733c28954c9e6
#: 4793b0d84c644d5393963481cdfe6de6
msgid "Range"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:111
#: 46e47c1789434113a6a47e44fe5c4c84
msgid "RC control range varies greatly depending on system used, installation, antennas used, terrain, and even weather conditions. But in general, for discussion purposes here, RC systems can be categorized into Short Range (2km and under) , Medium (2-10km) and Long Range (>10km). In addition, they may offer uni-directional (Vehicle to Transmitter) or bi-directional (Vehicle to/from Transmitter) telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:114
#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:134
#: 0971de7eada74dab8c35e94dba96c197
#: 7442f24f4f58468cbaeae5d324db9182
msgid "Telemetry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:116
#: 5fad1f5f5a004c60bc16d94d3bddc0bd
msgid "FrSky Horus Transmitter running Yaapu LUA script"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:120
#: a909dfa82b89448e9594a730e89066bc
msgid "Some systems provide transparent radio modems sending the telemetry from the autopilot, and others have proprietary protocols. Those with proprietary protocols often have means of displaying  telemetry data on the transmitter display itself, like FRSky or `OpenTX <https://www.open-tx.org/>`__ based Transmitters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:122
#: 83d48927ac444e129dbedb006cb3b181
msgid "Telemetry speeds vary from 56K to 1-2K baud depending on protocol and, in some cases, distance. Often telemetry range will be less than radio control range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:124
#: 202df417c3a54f2aaae48914d7a21bc6
msgid "Consult"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:127
#: bbf134fdeee745738710bd64b7bf387b
msgid "Number of channels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:129
#: e1aeff67320849d2a157b87b3befed03
msgid "ArduPilot requires at least 5 channels for most vehicles, however, 8 to 16 channels are commonly available in most systems and are very convenient for controlling other vehicle functions such as cameras or flight feature options. Many vehicles require 8 channels just for basic operation, such as many QuadPlanes."
msgstr ""

